   "id": "chem.acid-base-review",
   "name": "Unit 1 summary",
   "requires": [],
   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "Acids and bases are defined three ways: Arrhenius (H⁺ and OH⁻ in water), Brønsted–Lowry (proton donor and acceptor) and Lewis (electron-pair acceptor and donor). Kw = [H₃O⁺][OH⁻] = 1.0 × 10⁻¹⁴ links acidity to pH and pOH. Ka and Kb measure weak acid and base strength; buffers, salt hydrolysis, indicators and titrations all follow from these equilibria."
    },
    "am": {
     "text": "አሲድና ቤዝ በሦስት መንገድ ይገለጻሉ። Kw፣ pH፣ Ka እና Kb የአሲድ–ቤዝ ሚዛንን ይገልጻሉ። ባፈር፣ ሃይድሮሊሲስ፣ አመልካችና ቲትሬሽን ከዚህ ይከተላሉ።",
     "machine": true
    }
   },
